  {
   "id": "rjP-oAfbBAAJ",
   "from": "Daniel Hicks",
   "author": "5f533b50135a7f86",
   "date": "2019-10-07T20:36:21Z",
   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: lme function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hi Rachael (and everyone else), <div><br></div><div>The developer of lme4 explains why p-values aren’t reported here:  </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><a href=\"https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-help/2006-May/094765.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-help/2006-May/094765.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465694459000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2drwTsXFUoJ92O_bo--vPP\">https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-help/2006-May/094765.html</a></div><div><br></div></blockquote>There’s a complementary explanation here:  <blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><a href=\"https://bbolker.github.io/mixedmodels-misc/glmmFAQ.html#testing-hypotheses\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://bbolker.github.io/mixedmodels-misc/glmmFAQ.html%23testing-hypotheses&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465694459000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0qz3HRtPPb-3N5agHTck58\">https://bbolker.github.io/mixedmodels-misc/glmmFAQ.html#testing-hypotheses</a></div><div><br></div></blockquote>Both of these discussions are pretty technical — I’ll admit that I don’t fully understand them.  But, insofar as I do understand them, they argue that the error distributions for multilevel models are often much, much more complicated than the error distributions for plain linear regression (especially when they’re fit using REML rather than maximum likelihood).  Computationally simple ways of estimating errors are only really appropriate to special cases; more robust methods are computationally involved (and so take longer); and even the more robust methods can break in non-obvious ways.  So, in the spirit of fire season, it seems like there should be Red Flag warnings around any p-values reported from a multilevel model.  <div><br></div><div>I don’t know the nlme package very well, so I don&#39;t know how it calculates p-values or how the authors of that package might respond to the arguments above.  </div><div><br></div><div>If you do want to generate p-values or the like for lmer() models, the lme4 docs include this page, listing various methods:  </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><a href=\"https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/lme4/versions/1.1-21/topics/pvalues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/lme4/versions/1.1-21/topics/pvalues&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465694459000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2UO5Afyl6T4drHhF4yuawi\">https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/lme4/versions/1.1-21/topics/pvalues</a></div><div><br></div></blockquote>Cheers, <div>Dan<br><div><div><div><div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">----<br>Daniel J. Hicks</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">Assistant Professor<br>Cognitive and Information Sciences</div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">University of California, Merced<br><br>&quot;Cautious, careful people, always casting about to preserve their reputation and social standing, never can bring about a reform. Those who are really in earnest must be willing to be anything or nothing in the world&#39;s estimation.&quot; -- Susan B. Anthony<br><br>Pronouns: they/them/their</div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On Oct 7, 2019, at 12:50 PM, Rachael Coon &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">rec...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
