    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\">Hi Evan,<div><br></div><div>Thank you for responding. I&#39;ve referenced the dataframe and the random effects variable correctly now based on your suggestions. I spoke with a labmate who pointed out that the lmer() function does not provide p-values, which I need for my repeated measures design. Here&#39;s what she suggested:</div><div><br></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
