     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><div><div><a style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span>&lt;Annotation 2019-10-07 124636.png&gt;</span></a><br></div><br><br></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\"><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div style=\"text-align:left\"><br></div><div>This is what I was looking for, but if you have alternative reasons for using lmer(), I&#39;m opening to hearing them.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks again,</div><div><br></div><div>Rachael</div><div><br></div><div>On Monday, October 7, 2019 at 11:59:04 AM UTC-7, Evan Eskew wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Rachael,<div><br></div><div>There are a few things going on here:</div><div><br></div><div>- I believe the function you&#39;re looking to use is &quot;lmer()&quot;, not &quot;lme()&quot;</div><div>- You need to explicitly specify your data within the function call (I&#39;m going to assume your data frame is called &quot;my_data_frame&quot;)</div><div>- If, as your random effects, you&#39;re looking to have varying intercepts by &quot;Animal_ID&quot;, you&#39;ll need to specify those like so in your model formula: &quot;(1|Animal_ID)&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>Thus, I think this should work for you:</div><div><br></div><div>LA &lt;- lmer(duration ~ Trt + TrialDay + Trt*Trialday + (1|Animal_ID), data = my_data_frame)<br></div><div><br></div><div>From there, I&#39;d recommend checking out the example code here: <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/lme4/vignettes/lmer.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/lme4/vignettes/lmer.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465694459000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0PVaREW3g8Q4Dxm-e_vuoV\">https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/lme4/vignettes/lmer.pdf</a></div><div><br></div><div>All my best,</div><div>Evan</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Oct 7, 2019 at 2:45 PM Rachael Coon &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">rec...@</a><a href=\"http://ucdavis.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ucdavis.edu/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465694459000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2pdsMkfwgqyYaowr3yYvYw\">ucdavis.edu</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m trying to use the lme function to run a mixed effects model.<div><br></div><div>My random effect variable is Animal_ID, my fixed effects are TrialDay, Trt, and the interaction of TrialDay and Trt. The outcome variable is duration of the Behavior, which is currently subset to Latencytoapproach.</div><div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/davis-rug/attach/4d5b86a443965/Annotation%202019-10-07%20113958.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1&amp;authuser=0\" alt=\"Annotation 2019-10-07 113958.png\" width=\"400\" height=\"103\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">Here&#39;s how I currently have my model set up:</p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">LA &lt;- lme(duration ~ Trt + TrialDay + Trt*Trialday, random = Animal_ID)<br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\">But I&#39;m receiving an error message:</p><p style=\"text-align:left;clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"clear:both\">Error in reStruct(random, REML = REML, data = NULL) : </p><p style=\"clear:both\">  object &#39;Animal_ID&#39; not found</p><p style=\"clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"clear:both\">What am I doing wrong? Please help! I&#39;m new to mixed models in R.</p><p style=\"clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"clear:both\">Thank you,</p><p style=\"clear:both\"><br></p><p style=\"clear:both\">Rachael</p><div><br></div></div><div><br></div>--<span> </span><br>Check out our R resources at<span> </span><a href=\"http://d-rug.github.io/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://d-rug.github.io/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465694459000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3zY63oeBopdiyhnpJ08iuS\">http://d-rug.github.io/</a><br>---<span> </span><br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Davis R Users&#39; Group&quot; group.<br>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to<span> </span><a rel=\"nofollow\">davi...@</a><a href=\"http://googlegroups.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://googlegroups.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465694459000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3E3zxXgAO8jaRWhOL6ca9j\">googlegroups.com</a>.<br>To view this discussion on the web visit<span> </span><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/davis-rug/8db5810d-0068-48a8-b107-8896bc1b80af%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/davis-rug/8db5810d-0068-48a8-b107-8896bc1b80af%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465694459000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Mn-bZC69WS1McTIOy4Is8\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/davis-rug/8db5810d-0068-48a8-b107-8896bc1b80af%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br></blockquote></div><br clear=\"all\"><div><br></div>--<span> </span><br><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">Evan Eskew<div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><div><a href=\"http://eveskew.github.io/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://eveskew.github.io/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792465694459000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3QzWm6XrE9-3-xNf9H2QEH\">eveskew.github.io</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
